:"Which security posture a client is registered under (X5.1). This is the FAPI “one switch”."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"FAPI 2.0 is not a single feature but a bundle of constraints — mandatory PAR, mandatory PKCE"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"S256"},{"text":", mandatory strong client authentication, mandatory sender-constrained tokens,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a refusal of every relaxation the base specs permit. Encoding them as one profile rather","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than a dozen independent booleans means an operator cannot register a client that is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"nearly"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" FAPI, and a reviewer can answer “is this client financial-grade?” by reading one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"field. The same philosophy as the rate-limit postures: ordinary clients see no behaviour","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change at all, because ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"Self::Standard"},{"text":" is the serde default and every row","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written before schema v38 decodes to it.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ClientProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/ClientProfile/init(rawValue:)":{"abstract":[],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"?(","kind":"text"},{"text":"rawValue","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfil